#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:6
#: 126b8d7f5aa54ef9af05c7dd166c3d88
msgid "Airbrakes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:8
#: 269c2cde3db8420eb097da8cd9ee7e4e
msgid "`Airbrakes <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_brake_(aeronautics)>`__ are control surfaces that primarily add drag to your aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:10
#: 1da8c76eb6f842a9b3cf4b644b4b8aaa
msgid "These control surfaces can be driven by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:12
#: f8e91c54cc5044e1b40a029b4332376b
msgid "manual input via an RC channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:13
#: 906fd5f9576c40508a51e9c9be34a07f
msgid "automatic airbrake control, especially useful for steeper and more accurate automatic landing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:14
#: 0b12b51be3d54839bd6e026e3596711e
msgid "a combination of both, in which case the greater value is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:17
#: 7b23f0416c7840db95ec064d240fe14b
msgid "Servo Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:19
#: 0c53e8227ee0490ea8871c4fd6090e05
msgid "Connect the airbrake servo to a servo output channel on your autopilot. Set the corresponding servo output function to Airbrake (110). Set the servo minimum value SERVOX_MIN to the value for airbrake fully retracted. Set the maximum value SERVOX_MAX to the value for airbrake fully deployed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:24
#: 7747e62418434004bf93fb3a47e9b452
msgid "RC Channel Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:26
#: 2cfa9cc5d5404b3db53436fb77723e94
msgid "Assign a spare RC channel on your transmitter to a dial, slider or 3 position switch. On the autopilot, ensure this channel is calibrated and assign this channel the RC channel ``RCx_OPTION`` option Airbrake (210)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:32
#: 5b10c178f2f84d838c15cbd49610ced7
msgid "Automatic Airbrake Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:34
#: 451a9fc7dfd2492bbf8cf2b313687edb
msgid "You can have airbrakes automatically used in an automated landing or in conjunction with :ref:`Reverse Thrust<reverse-thrust-setup>` operation during certain throttled controlled modes or automatic landings and throttle-controlled descents, such as CRUISE mode while soaring. If manual control of reverse thrust has been enabled using the ``RCX_OPTION`` (64) or airbraking while in final flare in automatic landing using reverse thrust, then the airbrake deployment will be the greater of either the automatic demand or manual control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:37
#: aecfee77021046428ba7ee758c2334d2
msgid "Use With Reverse Thrust on Motor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:39
#: ac21472592154f1ab74fe76a1f19b067
msgid "Setup :ref:`Reverse Thrust<reverse-thrust-setup>` as desired. Airbrake operation will be in sync with reverse throttle applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:42
#: f22e3640d8a444feb9f28ab970f94859
msgid "Use Without Reverse Thrust ESC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:44
#: ac1fb2fdb2be4cc0ac3b7a1477cdf951
msgid "Same as above, however:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/airbrakes-on-plane.rst:46
#: 280a43020c1740d7a9a7eb7e8379fa64
msgid "Set :ref:`SERVO3_TRIM<SERVO3_TRIM>` = :ref:`SERVO3_MIN<SERVO3_MIN>` assuming SERVO 3 output is the throttle. This will assure that low stick and minimum demanded throttle is always SERVOx_MIN."
msgstr ""
